Direct-running the test files works. Great, so verification strategy:
- For scrum/team-hub/workbench: `node <file>` directly on test files (self-contained).
- For plugins tests that import ../lib/index.js: first build plugins lib with tsc (tsc doesn't need spawn; it's in-process node script). But plugins tests spawn `taskctl` and `git` via spawnSync with pipes... which will EPERM. Hmm — worker-regression tests use spawnSync('git') with piped stdio (helper git()). Under sandbox spawn EPERM. But slice-orchestration/worker-regression are EXISTING tests that used to pass in the CI... Evidence of T-0xx running them... They ran in a host without sandbox. In our sandbox these will fail at spawn EPERM unless spawn allowed. Wait — my probe A failed due to quoting, not necessarily EPERM. Let me test a genuine node spawnSync of git in a clean script file to see whether spawning is allowed at all under workspace-write.

Actually the node --test failure says `spawn EPERM` for the test runner's child process. But node --test spawns with `stdio: ['pipe','pipe','pipe']` (pipes!). Per tool docs, capturing piped stdio from another program through Node child_process.spawn fails with EPERM. That matches. So node --test EPERM because of pipes, not spawn itself. spawnSync git with default pipe → EPERM too. But we can call git through pwsh commands instead (pwsh pipeline allowed) — tests can't rely on that though since they're programmatic.

For plugins tests (doc-contract, artifact-register), avoid git spawning in tests. But the plugin itself (index.ts) uses runGit for worktree management; in our plugin tests we can set isolate:false so worktreeDir stays null → no git; the auto-register flows then read files from the workspace dir directly (cwd = workspace root). For doc-contract/artifact-register tests I'll write them to use isolate:false & local hub-mock & workspace fixture so no git spawn. For existence check we read from repoRootFor() (which = config.repoRoot when spaceBinding null) and worktreeDir = null → use repoRootFor as base. Hmm — S2 registers based on the worktree dir when isolate=true; test with isolate=false: done settle path for stage with next → autoPromote... autoPromote only runs when worktreeDir != null. If isolate=false and pipeline stage with next, then merged = true (worktreeDir null → merged=true) — fine.

But artifact-register test needs the settle path for a requirement task: stage.role = 'requirement', next='researcher' — pipeline mode, worker report done → commitWorktree skipped (worktreeDir null) → recordPatch skipped → recordArtifact worker artifact (nil in our report) → autoPromote true → stage.gate? requirement stage... in fixture roles.json we create requirement stage with gate:true? Hmm the current roles.json requirement has no gate. Actually RESEARCH K3 default = "soft gate: missing contract doc → stop in_review; when doc present, non-gate stages flow normally". requirement currently is non-gate → after registering, should advance to done then advancePipeline creates researcher task.

Wait S2 fixture acceptance: "fixture 回放 requirement 岗 done：结算后任务记录 artifacts 追加 docs/REQUIREMENTS.md 条目... worker 报告未填 artifact 亦登记 (AC-R1-2)"; "reviewer 岗结算把 {taskId} 解析为 docs/review/T-0xx-REVIEW.md 实际登记 (AC-R1-3)"; "契约文档缺失时任务停在 in_review 不误判成功流转且评论含期望路径与已登记清单的明确提示 (AC-R1-4)..."; "gate 岗 researcher 既有行为不回归：文档存在时登记后仍走 in_review 人工验收评论，缺失走缺失提示 (AC-R1-5)"; "coder 零登记 + 自填 artifact 不回退"; "登记先于 autoPromote"; "双写两分支（hub mock / taskctl argv）"; "幂等与多轮追加".

So the auto-registration runs in settle (done) for EVERY pipeline stage that has contract docs (stage.docs), regardless of gate. Where exactly? In runWorker, after commitWorktree and recordPatch, before recordArtifact/report? Actually the registration must occur before autoPromote (worktree deleted). Order in runWorker's done branch:

```
if (worktreeDir !== null) await commitWorktree(...)
await recordPatch(...)
if (report.artifact...) await recordArtifact(...)   // worker self-declared
if (isPipeline && stage && stage.next) {
